## 7. Form Inputs and Labels

- Every form field must have an associated `<label>` (Carbon provides this via the `labelText` prop)
- `ProgressBar` requires a non-empty `label` prop — never pass `label=""`

```jsx
// ❌ BAD — no accessible name
<ProgressBar label="" hideLabel value={50} max={100} />

// ✅ GOOD — label provides accessible name; hideLabel hides it visually if needed
<ProgressBar label="Sign-up progress" helperText="50% complete" value={50} max={100} />
```

---

## 8. Heading Hierarchy

Headings must follow a logical descending order within each page or section.
Do not skip levels.

```
h1  — Page title (one per page)
  h2  — Major section or option card title
    h3  — Sub-section title (e.g. step name inside a demo card)
      h4  — Assessment sub-headings (Pros / Cons)
```

When using Carbon's `<Heading>` component, always pass an explicit `as` prop —
without a `Section` context wrapper, the default level is unpredictable.

```jsx
// ❌ BAD — level depends on Section context which may not exist
<Heading>Progress Bar Designs</Heading>

// ✅ GOOD — explicit semantic level
<Heading as="h1" className="pip-page-title">Progress Bar Designs</Heading>
<Heading as="h2" id="opt1-title" className="pip-option-title">Vertical Step Tracker</Heading>
```

---

## 9. Icon Accessibility

Carbon icons require an `aria-label` when used as standalone meaningful elements.
When an icon is decorative (accompanied by visible text), it should be hidden.

```jsx
// ✅ Standalone icon — label required
<CheckmarkFilled aria-label="Step complete" size={16} />

// ✅ Icon beside visible text — hide the icon
<Button renderIcon={ArrowRight} iconDescription="Go to next step">Next</Button>

// ✅ Decorative icon in a list — sr-only text carries meaning
<CheckmarkFilled size={16} aria-hidden="true" />
<span className="sr-only">complete</span>
```

