## 10. Color Contrast (WCAG 1.4.3)

Minimum contrast ratios:
- **Normal text** (< 18pt / < 14pt bold): **4.5:1**
- **Large text** (≥ 18pt / ≥ 14pt bold): **3:1**
- **UI components and focus indicators**: **3:1**

Always use semantic design tokens — never hardcode hex colors.
See `.builder/rules/theme-contrast-guidelines.mdc` for the full list of safe
token pairs.

```scss
// ❌ BAD — hardcoded colors break in dark mode
.step-label { color: #161616; }

// ✅ GOOD — token adapts to light/dark theme automatically
.step-label { color: var(--text-primary); }
```

---

## 11. Keyboard Navigation

- All interactive elements must be reachable and operable via keyboard
- Use Carbon's Button component rather than `<div onClick>` — Carbon manages focus, keyboard events, and roles automatically
- Do not suppress default focus outlines; use `outline-color: var(--interactive-primary)` to style them on-brand

```jsx
// ❌ BAD — div is not keyboard focusable or screen-reader actionable
<div className="step-dot" onClick={handleClick}>3</div>

// ✅ GOOD — Button handles focus, Enter, Space, and ARIA role
<Button kind="ghost" onClick={handleClick}>Step 3</Button>
```

---

## 12. Performance — Static Data Outside Components

Static arrays or objects defined inside a React component are recreated on every
render. Move them to module scope.

```jsx
// ❌ BAD — STEPS recreated on every render
export default function MyPage() {
  const STEPS = [
    { key: 'personal', label: 'Personal Info' },
    { key: 'address',  label: 'Address' },
  ];
  ...
}

// ✅ GOOD — created once at module load
const STEPS = [
  { key: 'personal', label: 'Personal Info' },
  { key: 'address',  label: 'Address' },
];

export default function MyPage() {
  ...
}
```

This also applies to static config objects, comparison row data, option name
arrays, and any other value that does not depend on props or state.

---

## 13. Key Props — Avoid Array Index

Using array index as a `key` causes React to incorrectly reuse DOM nodes when
lists reorder or filter. Always use a stable, unique string.

```jsx
// ❌ BAD — index key causes subtle bugs when list order changes
{rows.map((row, i) => <tr key={i}>...</tr>)}

// ✅ GOOD — stable key from data
{rows.map((row) => <tr key={row.id}>...</tr>)}

// ✅ GOOD — compound key when no id is available
{rows.map((row, i) => (
  row.scores.map((score, j) => (
    <td key={`${row.label}-${j}`}>{score}</td>
  ))
))}
```

